          "site_admin": false
        },
        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:54Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:54Z",
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "body": "I don't make the distinction between a python-library or a python-application, as long as there is a lock-file.\nIMHO the distinction comes from not properly packaging applications.\n\nFor me an applications is\n - a python-package\n - config-file(s)\n - entry-point to execute/start\n\nIn scripts with inline metadata, distributed without a lock-file, the upper bounds make sense.",
